// Code signing for a device build. The team identifier is not committed: it goes in
// Signing.local.xcconfig, which is gitignored, and this file picks it up if it is there.
//
//   echo 'DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345' > app/Signing.local.xcconfig
//
// The team identifier of a free Apple ID is in Xcode > Settings > Accounts, or in
// ~/Library/MobileDevice/Provisioning Profiles once Xcode has signed once.
//
// Choosing the team in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab instead writes it into the project file,
// which the next `xcodegen generate` throws away; this survives that.
// With no such file the build is unsigned, which is all a simulator needs.

// The build number. One is enough for a build that only ever lands on a phone here; Xcode Cloud replaces it
// with its own, which counts up, by writing the file included below. A later definition wins in an xcconfig,
// which is why the include comes last.
CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION = 1

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
